<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">on&nbsp;canon</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">on&nbsp;canon</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Stuff like PIIs and ED-K is from my Broken Masquerade stuff and more directly my <a href="/amnesticization">Doomsday Contest</a> stuff. It's not necessary to read that stuff to understand this &#8212; that's what the footnotes are for &#8212; though some of that universe is crosslinked in here for good measure.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">In terms of the canon this establishes/would potentially establish as 4000, I do not think that all SCPs set after 4000 need to be set in the 2040s, don't worry. The specific number 4000 could have been out of range for a number of reasons, and I emphasize 'there is no canon' when it comes to each SCP's place in the universe.</span></p>
<p><sub>Ha-ha, Trauss took sixty-nine.</sub></p>
<p><sub>And we're in a 2040s AU where the 4000s are out of range I guess. IDK I'll think up some bullshit to explain it</sub></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">on&nbsp;history</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">because&nbsp;a&nbsp;few&nbsp;reviewers&nbsp;said&nbsp;people&nbsp;might&nbsp;not&nbsp;get&nbsp;the&nbsp;theme&nbsp;connection</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The SCP-4069 experience is the history of the Foundation, experienced by individual personnel through the eyes of other individual personnel, no matter the time period. Edit: And it's also <em>page</em> history, which I did not even think of, so thank you <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tl333s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304786); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1304786&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1534313369" alt="TL333s" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1304786)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tl333s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304786); return false;">TL333s</a></span> for pointing that out downthread.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">image&nbsp;info</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">image&nbsp;info</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Images are created by me in full. Released under CC-by-SA-3.0.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>SCP-4069-B is the Foundation. Put more clinically, it's the physical embodiment and representation of how the affected employee sees the Foundation and its influence on their life; hence, its appearance varies greatly and its behavior is neutral-to-hostile, occasionally kind, with neutrality and silent observation being the most common.</p>
<p>SCP-4069-A is its own place. It does its own thing. Sure, <em>most</em> of the time it will take the affected person to a random point in history at or near the death of a different Foundation employee, but some of 51174's logs are original events unique to SCP-4069-A. (Which ones are which is up to you to decide. Whatever forces are behind 4069 wouldn't want you to know the difference.) What does it mean that 4069-A generates Foundation-themed events? Beats me, but given the PII's implications&#8230; I'd say it's all in your head.</p>
</div>
</div>
